# Test: each page loads the assets its own markup needs, and no others
# VALIDATES: AC-8 and AC-11 of spec-web-htmx4-prepare -- the head block renders
#            the set scripts/codegen/web_assets.go derived from the markup that
#            page reaches, so a page rendering no htmx attribute loads no htmx
# PREVENTS: the union shipping to every page, and the opposite failure. A page
#           missing an asset it needs still renders and still answers 200, and
#           only the browser sees that nothing works.
#
# The sign-in page renders no htmx attribute at all: its form is a plain POST.
# The workbench renders several, so it loads the library.
#
# option=auth forces real authentication, so an unauthenticated GET renders the
# sign-in page rather than redirecting. web-i18n-fr.wb carries the same note.

option=timeout:value=30s
option=auth:user=admin:password=ze-web-admin

action=open:path=/login
expect=element:id=username
expect=head:not-contains=htmx.min.js

action=login:user=admin:password=ze-web-admin
action=open:path=/
expect=element:text=bgp
expect=head:contains=/assets/htmx.min.js
